"difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $Y\\sim\\mathcal{N}(0,\\sigma^2)$ with $\\sigma>0$ and density $f_Y$, and let $X=|Y|$. Which is the density of $X$?","options":["$f_Y(x)$ for $x\\ge0$, and $0$ for $x<0$","$2f_Y(x)$ for every real $x$","$2f_Y(x)$ for $x\\ge0$, and $0$ for $x<0$","$f_Y(x)$ for every real $x$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"694bca6e90415a9963cc240a","time_limit":40},{"id":"pt_batch8_folded_normal_distribution_011_curated20261027_003","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $Y\\sim\\mathcal{N}(\\mu,\\sigma^2)$ with $\\mu>0$, $\\sigma>0$, and $X=|Y|$. For $0<a<b$, let $p_+=\\mathbb{P}(a<Y\\le b)$ and $p_-=\\mathbb{P}(-b\\le Y<-a)$. What is $\\mathbb{P}(a<X\\le b)$?","options":["$p_+$","$2p_+$","$p_+-p_-$","$p_++p_-$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3d2f0742a239cf43c65d61d6","time_limit":30},{"id":"pt_batch8_folded_normal_distribution_016_curated20261027_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $Y\\sim\\mathcal{N}(\\mu,\\sigma^2)$ with $\\sigma>0$, and suppose only $X=|Y|$ is recorded. What information about $Y$ is lost?","options":["The sign of $Y$","The magnitude of $Y$","The randomness of $Y$, since $|Y|$ is constant","Nothing, since $Y$ can be recovered from $|Y|$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9fae871c4e6cc3fa744e0587","time_limit":30},{"id":"pt_batch8_folded_normal_distribution_019_curated20261027_005","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Let $Y\\sim\\mathcal{N}(\\mu,\\sigma^2)$ with $\\sigma>0$ and $X=|Y|$. What is $\\mathbb{P}(X<0)$?","options":["$\\tfrac{1}{2}$","$\\mathbb{P}(Y<0)$","$0$","It depends on $\\mu$ and $\\sigma$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"29c38a0d2526d3f77c25e10f","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_1b_probability_theory_for_eor_folded_normal_distribution_d452dc9a_topup20261028_001","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $Y_1\\sim\\mathcal{N}(2,1)$ and $Y_2\\sim\\mathcal{N}(-2,1)$, and let $X_1=|Y_1|$ and $X_2=|Y_2|$. Which statement about $X_1$ and $X_2$ is correct?","options":["$X_2$ tends to be smaller than $X_1$, since $Y_2$ tends to be smaller than $Y_1$.","$X_2$ is half-normal, since almost all mass of $Y_2$ lies below $0$ and is reflected.","$X_1$ and $X_2$ have the same distribution, since $-Y_2\\sim\\mathcal{N}(2,1)$ and $|Y_2|=|-Y_2|$.","$\\mathbb{P}(X_2\\le1)=\\mathbb{P}(Y_2\\le1)$, since folding changes only the negative values."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"8bb3d05ad4bff45f78230fbe","time_limit":50},{"id":"year_1_1b_probability_theory_for_eor_folded_normal_distribution_d452dc9a_topup20261028_002","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $Y\\sim\\mathcal{N}(1,4)$, a normal variable with mean $1$ and variance $4$, and let $X=|Y|$. What is $\\mathbb{E}[X^2]$?","options":["$4$","$17$","$10$","$5$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"8ad6ea13040b584686581372","time_limit":30}]}}